</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/ivan/ontologies/2024/0/ontomat#K">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#LargeMTSphereElement"/>
</rdf:Description>
<!-- Detection classes: what the reasoner infers from a plan -->
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#FElementSystem">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#DFTSystem"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A system containing at least one f-element (lanthanide/actinide): JUDFT_WARN_ONLY required, 4f occupation fluctuation in SCF is normal (pitfalls 8c, 9).</rdfs:comment>
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#DFTSystem"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasElement"/>
					<owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#HeavyElement"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#LargeSphereCationSystem">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#DFTSystem"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A system containing Ba/Cs/Rb/K: inpgen auto-assigns large MT spheres, differ 2 at setup without per-system sphere caps (pitfall 37).</rdfs:comment>
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#DFTSystem"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasElement"/>
					<owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#LargeMTSphereElement"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#NeedsJUDFTWarnOnly">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Task over an f-element system: JUDFT_WARN_ONLY is REQUIRED (pitfall 8c). Gate: hasMitigationJUDFTWarnOnly must be true, else INCONSISTENT.</rdfs:comment>
	<rdfs:subClassOf>
		<owl:Restriction>
			<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasMitigationJUDFTWarnOnly"/>
			<owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
		</owl:Restriction>
	</rdfs:subClassOf>
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasSystem"/>
					<owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#FElementSystem"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#NeedsSphereCaps">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Task over a Ba/Cs/Rb/K system: per-system MT-sphere caps REQUIRED (pitfall 37). Gates: hasMitigationSphereCaps AND hasPerSystemTemplates must both be true.</rdfs:comment>
	<rdfs:subClassOf>
		<owl:Restriction>
			<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasMitigationSphereCaps"/>
			<owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
		</owl:Restriction>
	</rdfs:subClassOf>
	<rdfs:subClassOf>
		<owl:Restriction>
			<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasPerSystemTemplates"/>
			<owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
		</owl:Restriction>
	</rdfs:subClassOf>
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasSystem"/>
					<owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#LargeSphereCationSystem"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#DirectFLEURSubmit">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
	<rdfs:comment>FLEUR task on the direct yascheduler API (no AiiDA staging): spawn must carry nohup and JUDFT_WARN_ONLY itself (pitfalls 31, 32). Gates: hasSpawnNohup AND hasMitigationJUDFTWarnOnly must both be true.</rdfs:comment>
	<rdfs:subClassOf>
		<owl:Restriction>
			<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasSpawnNohup"/>
			<owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
		</owl:Restriction>
	</rdfs:subClassOf>
	<rdfs:subClassOf>
		<owl:Restriction>
			<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasMitigationJUDFTWarnOnly"/>
			<owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
		</owl:Restriction>
	</rdfs:subClassOf>
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasEngine"/>
					<owl:hasValue rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#fleur"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasSubmitChannel"/>
					<owl:hasValue rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#DirectYaschedulerAPI"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#BroydenOnFLEUR62">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Broyden1/2 mixing requested on the FLEUR 6.2 build: NOT implemented, the engine errors at startup (pitfall 15). Flagged by classification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#BroydenOnFLEUR62">
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasMixingScheme"/>
					<owl:hasValue rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#Broyden1"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#Broyden2OnFLEUR62">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Same trap with Broyden2 (pitfall 15).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#Broyden2OnFLEUR62">
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasMixingScheme"/>
					<owl:hasValue rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#Broyden2"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#PRDApprovedPlan">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CampaignPlan"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A plan whose PRD the human approved. The only plan a run may start (reharness: the human approves the intent, never the graph).</rdfs:comment>
	<rdfs:subClassOf>
		<owl:Restriction>
		<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#prdApproved"/>
		<owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
	</owl:Restriction>
	</rdfs:subClassOf>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraSignatureBatch">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CampaignPlan"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A fast uniform 412 batch with every evaluator CalcJob at exit 0: infrastructure failure signature (pitfall 42). Never tune SCF parameters in response. hasAllTasksExit412 is a closed-world builder assertion (FaCT++ cannot classify into forall-defined classes).</rdfs:comment>
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#CampaignPlan"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasTask"/>
					<owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#TaskExit412"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasAllTasksExit412"/>
					<owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
				</owl:Restriction>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasBatchEvalExitZero"/>
					<owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:hasValue>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#AllTasksExit412">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CampaignPlan"/>
	<rdfs:comment>DEPRECATED indirection: FaCT++ realisation does not classify instances into forall-defined classes (verified empirically), so this class carries no equivalentClass axiom. The all-tasks-exit-412 check is a plan-bUILDER assertion (hasAllTasksExit412), asserted closed-world from the observed task states.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasAllTasksExit412">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CampaignPlan"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Closed-world plan-builder assertion: every task in the plan observed at exit family 412. Computed by the validator from task states, not inferred by the reasoner (FaCT++ cannot classify into forall-defined classes).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#TaskExit412">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A task whose observed exit-code family is 412.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#TaskExit412">
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#CalculationTask"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasExitCodeFamily"/>
					<owl:hasValue rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#exit_412"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<!-- ================= LAYER 3: EXPERIENCE (pitfall corpus) =========== -->
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalArtefact"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A class of engine failures with known detection, cause and fix.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Infrastructure failures: SSH drops, zombie processes, occupancy-poll bugs, spawn-channel hangup. Fix infrastructure; NEVER answer with SCF parameter tuning.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Physics-level failures: convergence, ghost states, MT-sphere confinement, basis set.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
</rdf:Description>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#ConvergenceFailureMode">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>SCF/geometry convergence.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#BasisSetFailureMode">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Basis-set problems: non-neutral cell, linear dependence, neighbor-list limits.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#InputPrepFailureMode">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Input-generation errors: XIncludes, latsys, primitive-vs-conventional cell.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#ConvergenceFailureMode">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#BasisSetFailureMode"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#ConvergenceFailureMode">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InputPrepFailureMode"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#BasisSetFailureMode">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InputPrepFailureMode"/>
</rdf:Description>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#DiagnosticsGap">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Failure modes with signature ambiguity: must cross-reference BOTH databases and read output files before routing (pitfall 24: DONE does not mean succeeded, at either layer).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#FsmStateKind">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalArtefact"/>
	<rdfs:comment>reharness FSM state kinds: where a fix routes. Decisions belong to FSM states, never to imperative runtime glue.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#FsmStateKind"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Deterministic code leaf: run the fix command, no tokens.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#agentState">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#FsmStateKind"/>
	<rdfs:comment>LLM judgment leaf: novel diagnosis, input authoring.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#approvalState">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#FsmStateKind"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Human approval gate: risky or policy-gated actions.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#waitState">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#FsmStateKind"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Poll an external signal: daemon process, yascheduler DB, output file.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#agentState"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#approvalState"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#waitState"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#agentState">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#approvalState"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#agentState">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#waitState"/>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#approvalState">
	<owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#waitState"/>
</rdf:Description>
<!-- Experience properties -->
<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasRouting">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#FsmStateKind"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Where the FSM routes a failure of this mode: code / agent / approval / wait.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>
<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasObservedExitCode">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#AiiDAExitCodeFamily"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Exit-code family typically observed for this failure mode.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>
<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasDetectedClass">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>The plan-level detection class that flags this failure mode pre-emptively (range: the detection classes above).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>
<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasPitfallRef">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Pitfall identifier in the collected experience (mpds-aiida skill taxonomy), e.g. 8c, 22b, 42-BSD.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>
<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasSignature">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Deterministic signature regexes (Python re syntax) matched against failure text.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>
<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasFix">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
	<rdfs:comment>The known fix: exact command or action, from the collected experience.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>
<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasEvidenceCommand">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#EngineFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Deterministic evidence-gathering command to run before concluding the mode.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>
<!-- The pitfall individuals -->
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_ghost_states">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ConvergenceFailureMode"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Ghost states from core electrons of f-elements abort the run. Warning escalated to fatal by default.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasObservedExitCode rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#exit_303"/>
	<hasDetectedClass rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#NeedsJUDFTWarnOnly"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">8c</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Too low eigenvalue detected</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Stage JUDFT_WARN_ONLY in the task dir before the engine run. AiiDA FleurCalculation stages it automatically (line 465-468 of calculation.fleur); direct yascheduler API must have touch JUDFT_WARN_ONLY in the spawn command.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_mt_sphere_confinement">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#BasisSetFailureMode"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>High-n s valence states cannot confine in inpgen-auto large MT spheres of Ba/Cs/Rb/K. Dominant mode behind dft.mpds.io geometry-optimization failures.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#agentState"/>
	<hasObservedExitCode rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#exit_303"/>
	<hasDetectedClass rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#NeedsSphereCaps"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">37</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">differ 2: problems with solving dirac equation</hasSignature>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">too few nodes</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Per-system MT-sphere radius caps via set_species (masci_tools): use EXACT species names from that system inp.xml (e.g. &quot;Barium (Ba)&quot;); caps live in per-system templates only, never shared base templates. Diagnose the failing species from the FLEUR &quot;out&quot; file, not from expectation.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_broyden_not_implemented">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InputPrepFailureMode"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>The InputSchema lists Broyden1/2 as valid imix values but the build errors at startup.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasDetectedClass rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#BroydenOnFLEUR62"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">15</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Broyden 1/2 method not implemented</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use Anderson mixing alpha=0.15 (or straight as last resort). Broyden1/Broyden2 are NOT implemented in the FLEUR 6.2 build.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_straight_too_conservative">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ConvergenceFailureMode"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>PR #20 straight-mixing scheme evaluated and REFUTED on SrTiO3/GdNi/NiZn.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#agentState"/>
	<hasObservedExitCode rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#exit_362"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">22b</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DID_NOT_CONVERGE</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Anderson alpha=0.15 (OLD scheme) converges NiZn in 17 iterations; straight alpha=0.05 stuck at 40-260 Htr. Straight-mixing 2x300 does NOT rescue 412/497 hard systems (attempt-2 reproduced attempt-1 exactly).</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_walltime_keyerror">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Truncated out.xml yields partial output_parameters; bracket access Excepts the SCF workchain.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasObservedExitCode rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#exit_497"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">35</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KeyError: 'walltime'</hasSignature>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">unsupported operand type\(s\) for -: 'NoneType' and 'NoneType'</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Guard parser-derived keys: output_parameters.get(&quot;walltime&quot;, 0) at scf.py line 696, and or 0 / .get(...) at every subtraction site in get_res. Patched in installed aiida_fleur (backup at .bak).</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_truncated_outxml">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Missing shell.out/out.error warnings are a RED HERRING: the parser only warns on those.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasObservedExitCode rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#exit_303"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">12</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The out.xml file is broken</hasSignature>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Repairing was not possible</hasSignature>
	<hasEvidenceCommand rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">sudo PGPASSWORD= /data/pg/bin/psql -h localhost -U postgres -d aiida -c &quot;...&quot; and yascheduler_tasks.metadata-&gt;&gt;error for SSH failure records; compare retrieved FolderData content</hasEvidenceCommand>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Root cause chain: SSH drop mid-write (pitfall 13/39) or spawn-channel hangup (pitfall 31) -&gt; truncated out.xml -&gt; masci_tools first parse consumes the handle at EOF (pitfall 33: wrap in seek(0)) -&gt; exit 303. Resubmit; check yascheduler metadata for the SSH failure before tuning anything.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_premature_done">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>DONE does not mean succeeded at either layer (pitfall 18/24).</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">13</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">no &lt;/fleurOutput&gt; closing tag</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Task marked DONE after 7-14 iterations on an SSH-unstable node. Cross-reference yascheduler_tasks.status=2 vs the AiiDA process state; resubmit; if persistent, disable the unstable node in yascheduler_nodes.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_spawn_channel_hangup">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Without nohup the engine dies after 1-3 SCF iterations; yascheduler still marks DONE.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasDetectedClass rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#DirectFLEURSubmit"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">31</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">completed after 1 iterations</hasSignature>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">truncated mid-iteration</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">nohup is REQUIRED in the yascheduler spawn command: run_bg creates the process on an SSH channel that is killed when the poll cycle reaps it. Never quote the live [engine.fleur] spawn from memory (pitfall 11): read it from /etc/yascheduler/yascheduler.conf.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_false_idle_occupancy">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>THE physics-vs-infra separation rule: verify evals ran before tuning SCF parameters.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasDetectedClass rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraSignatureBatch"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">42</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">uniform batch of fast 412s</hasSignature>
	<hasEvidenceCommand rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Verify evals actually ran: yac task rows for the eval calcjobs + iteration count in the retrieved out file, BEFORE tuning SCF parameters</hasEvidenceCommand>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">BSD ps vs GNU :255 occupancy poll bug: false-idle node polls rmtree live task dirs on Darwin; engines die silently RC=2. Fixed in installed yascheduler 1.8.1 (kit /data/fleur_campaign/patches/). A uniform fast-412 batch with eval exit 0 = infra, not physics.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_unit_cell_not_neutral">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#BasisSetFailureMode"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A basis problem, not a runtime issue: the cell is fine, the assigned bases are not.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#agentState"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">19</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">INPBAS \*\*\*\* UNIT CELL NOT NEUTRAL</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Basis set charge mismatch (MPDSBSL_NEUTRAL_6TH family): Yb-containing perovskites with certain oxidation states. Custom basis assignments or different oxidation states needed per composition.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_wbecke_neighbor_list">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#BasisSetFailureMode"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Public-keyword limitations on the Mac arm64 build.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#agentState"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">26</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">WBECKE_F NEIGHBOR LIST TOO BIG</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LIMBEK is absent from the CRYSTAL23 public build (like CYCLES: use MAXCYCLE). For covalent solids: HF has no Becke grid, but diffuse bases (pob-DZVP-rev2, 6-21G*) may then hit BASIS SET LINEARLY DEPENDENT. MgO DFT-PBE works; Si diamond needs HF.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_xinclude_not_flattened">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InputPrepFailureMode"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicsFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>yascheduler only ships input_files: un-flattened XIncludes reference missing files.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">XML document cannot be validated against Schema</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">inpgen emits xi:include tags (NOT self-closing: href=&quot;kpts.xml&quot;&gt; &lt;/xi:include&gt;). Flatten all XIncludes into one self-contained inp.xml before submitting directly; assert len(re.findall(xi:include, inp_xml)) == 0. AiiDA FleurinpData flattens automatically.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_unverified_method_claim">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#DiagnosticsGap"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Methodology gate: untested method claims route to human approval.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#approvalState"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">9</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Do NOT claim DFT+HIA/DFT+U is required for 4f systems without testing plain PBE first. GdNi: the actual issue was itmax 50 vs 200 and wrong alpha. 4f occupation fluctuation keeping distance at 1e-3..1e-4 is NORMAL; gate on held-out accuracy, not SatAgg (single-run sat is degenerate).</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_orte_resource_exhaustion">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Batch-vs-serial scheduling decision grounded in a measured crash rate.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">20</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ORTE_ERROR_LOG: Out of resource</hasSignature>
	<hasSignature rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">process killed \(SIGTERM\)</hasSignature>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Concurrent --oversubscribe Pcrystal tasks exhaust ORTE on small nodes: 17/37 crashed. Submit in batches of 5-10, match ncpus to physical cores, run campaigns serially.</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#pf_stale_waiting_wedge">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#InfraFailureMode"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Campaign driver precondition, checked pre-launch, not post-mortem.</rdfs:comment>
	<hasRouting rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#codeState"/>
	<hasObservedExitCode rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#exit_412"/>
	<hasPitfallRef rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">33</hasPitfallRef>
	<hasFix rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A stale waiting workchain of type fleur.mpds silently wedges the serial campaign driver: its submit gate counts active workchains. Clean waiting processes BEFORE launching a campaign (verdi process repair; kill remaining via ProcessNode set_exit_status(130) + seal; DROP the exit_status filter on sealed nodes).</hasFix>
</rdf:Description>
<!-- ============ NORTH-STAR: property-driven workflow synthesis ========= -->
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalWorkflow">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalArtefact"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A workflow (workchain composition) computing material properties. The subject of on-the-fly generation: the plan names a property; the ontology supplies the workflow that realizes it.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#WorkChainStep">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalArtefact"/>
	<rdfs:comment>One AiiDA workchain in a workflow composition.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_fleur_scf">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#WorkChainStep"/>
	<rdfs:comment>fleur.mpds SCF + geometry optimization (the campaign workhorse).</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_fleur_dos">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#WorkChainStep"/>
	<rdfs:comment>fleur.dos_seebeck: DOS + Seebeck from a converged SCF.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_crystal_scf">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#WorkChainStep"/>
	<rdfs:comment>crystal.mpds SCF (Pcrystal).</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_crystal_seebeck">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#WorkChainStep"/>
	<rdfs:comment>crystal.mpds_seebeck.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_phonon">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#WorkChainStep"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Phonon stage: FLEUR phonon workflow / CRYSTAL FREQCALC (+PREOPTGEOM INSIDE the FREQCALC block, never a sibling keyword).</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasTargetProperty">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CampaignPlan"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/ivan/ontologies/2024/0/ontomat#Property"/>
	<rdfs:comment>The material property the campaign computes — the hierarchy entry the plan is generated FROM.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>
<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#realizedBy">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/ivan/ontologies/2024/0/ontomat#Property"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalWorkflow"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A base Property individual is realized by this workflow (asserted additively on base individuals).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>
<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasStep">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalWorkflow"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#WorkChainStep"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Composition: a workflow runs these workchain steps.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#SeebeckWorkflow">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalWorkflow"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Seebeck coefficient: SCF convergence then DOS/Seebeck stage.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhononWorkflow">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalWorkflow"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Phonon spectrum; imaginary modes route back to geometry optimization (pitfalls 25/27).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#wf_fleur_seebeck">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#SeebeckWorkflow"/>
	<hasStep rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_fleur_scf"/>
	<hasStep rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_fleur_dos"/>
	<rdfs:comment>FLEUR route: fleur.mpds SCF then fleur.dos_seebeck.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#wf_crystal_seebeck">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#SeebeckWorkflow"/>
	<hasStep rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_crystal_scf"/>
	<hasStep rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_crystal_seebeck"/>
	<rdfs:comment>CRYSTAL route: crystal.mpds SCF then crystal.mpds_seebeck.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#wf_crystal_phonon">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhononWorkflow"/>
	<hasStep rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_crystal_scf"/>
	<hasStep rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#wc_phonon"/>
	<rdfs:comment>CRYSTAL FREQCALC with PREOPTGEOM inside the block.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#PropertyTargetedPlan">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#CampaignPlan"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A plan generated FROM a property-hierarchy entry (hasTargetProperty some base Property).</rdfs:comment>
	<owl:equivalentClass>
		<owl:Class>
			<owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
				<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#CampaignPlan"/>
				<owl:Restriction>
					<owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasTargetProperty"/>
					<owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/ivan/ontologies/2024/0/ontomat#Property"/>
				</owl:Restriction>
			</owl:intersectionOf>
		</owl:Class>
	</owl:equivalentClass>
</owl:Class>
<!-- ============ PHYSICS-DERIVATION LAYER ========================== -->
<owl:Class rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation">
	<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalArtefact"/>
	<rdfs:comment>A named solid-state physics equation, carried as data (hasLatexForm, hasSymPyForm) — NEVER as DL axioms: description logic cannot express calculus. The executable content lives in physics.py (SymPy) and the AiiDA workchains; the ontology carries the derivation structure and the workflow bindings.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>
<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#derivesFrom">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<rdfs:comment>The approximation relation: a derived equation derivesFrom a more fundamental one (Kohn-Sham derivesFrom Schroedinger). Transitive: chains of approximations compose; every equation here reaches eq_schroedinger in finitely many steps.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>
<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasDerivationLevel">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty"/>
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
	<rdfs:comment>Approximation level of the derivation (functional: one level per equation). exact / approximate / heuristic.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>
<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#computedBy">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#ComputationalWorkflow"/>
	<rdfs:comment>The executable workflow that computes the equation's quantities (realizedBy binds material properties to workflows; computedBy binds equations to them).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>
<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasLatexForm">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
	<rdfs:comment>MathJax-ready LaTeX of the equation, as typed in the literature.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>
<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#hasSymPyForm">
	<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
	<rdfs:comment>str() of the SymPy Eq in physics.py — byte-identical by construction; tests/test_physics_parity.py fails loud on drift.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_schroedinger">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<hasDerivationLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">exact</hasDerivationLevel>
	<hasLatexForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">\hat{H}\Psi = E\Psi</hasLatexForm>
	<hasSymPyForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Eq(H*Psi, E*Psi)</hasSymPyForm>
	<rdfs:comment>The time-independent Schrödinger equation — the ROOT of the physics-derivation DAG. Non-relativistic stationary-state quantum mechanics; every DFT quantity in this ontology is derived from it by the chain below.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_kohn_sham">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<derivesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_schroedinger"/>
	<hasDerivationLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">approximate</hasDerivationLevel>
	<hasLatexForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">\left(-\frac{1}{2}\nabla^2 + v_\mathrm{eff}\right)\psi_i = \varepsilon_i\psi_i</hasLatexForm>
	<hasSymPyForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Eq(psi_i*(-nabla**2/2 + v_eff), eps_i*psi_i)</hasSymPyForm>
	<rdfs:comment>The Kohn-Sham equations: exact-in-principle mapping of the interacting system onto non-interacting orbitals; approximations enter through the exchange-correlation functional.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_dft_energy">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<derivesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_schroedinger"/>
	<hasDerivationLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">approximate</hasDerivationLevel>
	<hasLatexForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">E[n] = T_s[n] + \int v_\mathrm{ext} n\,d\mathbf{r} + J[n] + E_\mathrm{xc}[n]</hasLatexForm>
	<hasSymPyForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FunctionalForm:E[n] = T_s[n] + Integral(v_ext*n, r) + J[n] + E_xc[n]</hasSymPyForm>
	<rdfs:comment>The DFT total-energy functional: the variational object the SCF cycle minimizes; the energy whose differences the EOS/MAE workflows fit. The SymPy form is the functional-equation spelling (not an Eq — DFT energy is a functional of the density).</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_hellmann_feynman">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<derivesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_kohn_sham"/>
	<hasDerivationLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">exact</hasDerivationLevel>
	<hasLatexForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">F_i = -\frac{\partial E}{\partial x_i}</hasLatexForm>
	<hasSymPyForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Eq(F, -Derivative(E, x))</hasSymPyForm>
	<rdfs:comment>Forces from the converged DFT total energy: the bridge from eq_dft_energy to geometry optimization and the fleur.forces workchain. Exact under Born-Oppenheimer (clamped nuclei) given an exactly converged density.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_birch_murnaghan">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<derivesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_dft_energy"/>
	<hasDerivationLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">heuristic</hasDerivationLevel>
	<hasLatexForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">E(V) = E_0 + \frac{9V_0B_0}{16}\left[\left(\frac{V_0}{V}-1\right)^3 B_0'+ \left(\frac{V_0}{V}-1\right)^2\left(6-4\frac{V_0}{V}\right)\right]</hasLatexForm>
	<hasSymPyForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Eq(E_c, 9*B_0*V_0*(B_0'*(-1 + V_0/V)**3 + (-1 + V_0/V)**2*(6 - 4*V_0/V))/16 + E_0)</hasSymPyForm>
	<rdfs:comment>3rd-order Birch-Murnaghan EOS: the analytic form fitted to the fleur.eos volume scan; its B_0 parameter IS the bulk modulus (prop_bulk_modulus).</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_mae_scan">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<derivesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_dft_energy"/>
	<hasDerivationLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">heuristic</hasDerivationLevel>
	<hasLatexForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">E(\phi) = E_0 + K_u \sin^2(\phi)</hasLatexForm>
	<hasSymPyForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Eq(E_phi, E_0 + K_u*sin(phi)**2)</hasSymPyForm>
	<rdfs:comment>Magnetization-rotation scan: the symmetry form the fleur.mae workchain fits; K_u = E(90°) − E(0°) is the anisotropy (prop_magnetic_anisotropy).</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_phonon_dispersion">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<derivesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_hellmann_feynman"/>
	<hasDerivationLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">heuristic</hasDerivationLevel>
	<hasLatexForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">\omega(k) = 2\sqrt{D/m}\,\left|\sin\left(\frac{ka}{2}\right)\right|</hasLatexForm>
	<hasSymPyForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Eq(omega, 2*sqrt(D)*Abs(sin(a*k/2))/sqrt(m))</hasSymPyForm>
	<rdfs:comment>Phonon dispersion (monatomic-chain form): the textbook form of the finite-displacement frequencies the phonopy.fleur route computes (prop_phonon_spectrum). The supercell force constants D come from eq_hellmann_feynman at displaced geometries.</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_seebeck_mott">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#PhysicalEquation"/>
	<derivesFrom rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_kohn_sham"/>
	<hasDerivationLevel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">approximate</hasDerivationLevel>
	<hasLatexForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">S = -\frac{\pi^2 k_B^2 T}{3e}\frac{d\ln\sigma(\varepsilon)}{d\varepsilon}\Big|_{\varepsilon_F}</hasLatexForm>
	<hasSymPyForm rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Eq(S, -3.96583751701583e-28*pi**2*T*Derivative(log(sigma_epsilon), epsilon))</hasSymPyForm>
	<rdfs:comment>Mott-form Seebeck: the degenerate-limit transport coefficient from the Kohn-Sham band structure (fleur.dos_seebeck; prop_seebeck).</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>
<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://mpds.io/ontology#eq_birch_murnaghan">
	<computedBy rdf:resource="https://mpds.io/ontology#wf_fleur_eos"/>
</rdf:Description>
